% SCHERZO RETURNS, bars 265-300 (Tempo I).
% 265-280: theme A as at 13, but Vln II pizzicato and Fl 1 doubling the violins heterophonically two octaves up (pp, with turns and passing notes).
% 281-288: the counterstatement compressed: Ob 1 calls (281), the strings answer in E minor on V (283-284 = 31-32), then 41-44 a minor third lower: V7 of E, f (Vln II arco).
% 289-300: the second idea in E minor, as at 121-132 (c003: the reprise stays in the tonic, as Dvorak 9/iii's return does; the G-major version is heard once, at 45).

